  "content": {
    "title": "How to watch new 'DTF St. Louis' episodes as suspects shift",
    "text": "March 21, 2026, 3:00 p.m. ETSpoiler alert! This story includes details from Episodes 1 - 3 of HBO's \"DTF St. Louis.\"As with most whodunnits, the suspect keeps shifting at every turn and as Episode 3 of HBO's \"DTF St. Louis\" drew to an end, viewers were left confused if Carol (Linda Cardellini) was behind husband Floyd's (David Harbour) death or if it was best friend Clark (Jason Bateman), with whom Carol was having an affair.Carol and Clark's affair may have begun harmlessly, but it later appears that feelings became involved and Carol began to increasingly rely on Clark for emotional support and otherwise.It doesn't help that Clark, a successful weatherman \"struggling with the banality of middle age and a sparkless marriage,\" introduced Floyd to DTF, which stands for \"down to (expletive),\" a dating app intended for those who are looking to \"spice up\" their married lives, shortly before the latter died.HBO says the show is about a \"love triangle between three adults experiencing middle-age malaise that leads to one of them ending up dead.\"\"DTF St. Louis\" creator Steven Conrad told People the show was inspired by his own personal experiences, when he began to see people around him \"feel emotional desperation and then make bad decisions\" in their middle age.\"I'm in my middle age, and most of my friends are too, and, somehow or another, it's another phase of life where people make terrible decisions,\" Conrad told the media outlet. \"The first one's 14, and no one wants to live through that again. But that same misguided, desperate need to fit in or to find someone to feel safe, it comes back around in middle age, and it can lead to bad decision-making.\"Here's what to know about when new \"DTF St. Louis\" episodes release and how to watch them.When do new episodes of 'DTF St. Louis' come out?Episode 4 of \"DTF St. Louis\" will air on HBO on Sunday, March 22, at 9 p.m. ET / PT and will be available to stream on HBO Max at the same time, with new episodes dropping weekly on Sundays.The season finale is scheduled for Sunday, April 12.How to watch new 'DTF St. Louis' episodesThe seven-episode season will air on HBO at 9 p.m. ET / 6 p.m. PT on Sundays and will be available to stream on HBO Max at the same time.Watch 'DTF St. Louis' on HBO Max with SlingNeed a news break? Check out the all-new PLAY hub with puzzles, games and more!Watch 'DTF St. Louis' trailer'DTF St. Louis' castThe cast for \"DTF St. Louis,\" according to HBO, includes:Jason Bateman as Clark ForrestDavid Harbour as FloydLinda Cardellini as CarolRichard Jenkins as Detective HomerJoy Sunday as Jodie PlumbSaman Shafiq is a trending news reporter for USA TODAY. Reach her at sshafiq@usatodayco.com and follow her on X and Instagram @saman_shafiq7.",
